# Recipes

## Shape

```yaml
id: youtube-thumbnail            # kebab-case, matches the file name
version: 1                       # bump on any output-affecting change
summary: Image in, 1280x720 YouTube thumbnail out.
requires:
  photocraft: { min: "0.23.0", commands: [ "<ids read from photocraft-cli commands>" ] }
inputs:
  image: { type: file, formats: [jpg, png, webp, psd, tif] }
  title: { type: text, max_words: 5 }
preset: presets/youtube.yaml     # sizes, max bytes, colour space — never inline magic numbers
steps:
  - id: compose
    app: photocraft
    mode: headless-mcp           # one-shot | headless-mcp  (live is never allowed in recipes)
    commands: [ … ]              # ids + params exactly as the installed app documents them
    outputs: { psd: out/thumbnail.psd }
  - id: export
    …
verify:
  - { file: out/thumbnail.jpg, width: 1280, height: 720, max_bytes: 2000000, colorspace: srgb }
  - { preview: [ [168, 94], [320, 180] ], sheet: out/previews.png }
```

## Rules

- Command IDs and params come from `apps/<app>/<version>.json` (generated). Never invent one; if a needed command doesn't exist, the recipe can't use it — open a feature request (see `upstream-contrib.mdc`) and design a fallback step.
- Every recipe has at least one verifier per output file and produces a preview an agent can look at.
- Recipes only write inside the job dir; inputs are read through read roots.
- Warnings from apps (missing fonts, dropped content) fail the step unless the recipe explicitly allows that warning with a reason.
- Templates in `templates/` are our own work; record provenance in `templates/README.md`.
- A new or changed recipe ships with `docs/recipes/<id>.md` and a dry run (`sc run <id> --dry-run`) plus one live run on the Mac before it is called done.
- Keep recipes small and composable; a recipe may call another recipe as a step.
